 are  going to start an attack now a lot of  times black in this position there's two  different moves we're going to go over  right now a lot of times black will try  to get the knight out of there and they  will try to initiate a move to make  white move so first we move you may see  is just simply pawn to h6 attacking the  knight here the knight obviously can't  go back to h3 he'll be take in can't go  to f3 he'll be taken that can't go to e4  because of his piece there can't go to e  6 or he'll be taken and his other move  is f7 so black right away is basically  saying move your knight we're actually  going to have a another sacrifice here  and we're going to attack the f7 square  and for many people that have studied  chest they know that the f7 Square is a  very big weakness for black and so we  were going to go ahead and take it and  then when black recaptures you already  see blacks entire defense around his  King is gone and his King is in a very  bad position now eventually we can bring  our Bishop out here to c4 in check get  our bishop involved we also want to get  our queen involved on g4 anytime black  tries to defend his pawn at the  beginning you always always want to get  your Queen to g4 the Queen on g4 is just  devastating for many reasons so if we  look at we need to decide which one  we're going to do first and if you look  at it if Bishop to c4 first black can  easily come down with his pawn  to d5 and block and at the same time his  Bishop on c8 is now defending the pawn  on g4 and obviously since we want to get  our Queen to g4 that's not going to be  our first move our first move we're not  going to put them in check yet we're  going to go ahead and take on g4 now the  Queen is very active he can do a lot of  things and so Black has to try to figure  out how to stop this attack we have many  different options that we have we can  always come in the future bring our  Bishop into the attack c4 once we bring  our Bishop into the attack as you c